Scope resolution operator (::)
it is used to access the variable ,function ,or class member that belongs to a particular scope 
it tells the compiler which scope (global,class,or namespace) a particular identifier belongs to 


scope_name::identifier

:: — used to access something from an outer scope when it's hidden by an inner scope.

Usage	Example	Meaning
Global scope	::value	Access global variable when local/class variable has same name
Class scope	ClassName::method()	Define or access static members of a class
Namespace scope	std::cout	Access something from a namespace


